`uuid  last-active  project  title`. Older transcripts are on disk too and are
fair game if the answer is not in this list:

{candidates}

**Return your answer by calling StructuredOutput**, with `sessions` set to the
matching session uuids, best first, at most 5 — each with `why` (one line:
what was discussed there, and when) and `confidence` — and `answer` set to a
few sentences on what you found, carrying the concrete details from the
session (decisions, numbers, hostnames, file paths) so that I may not need to
reopen it at all. If nothing matches, return an empty `sessions` list and say
so in `answer`. Do not answer in prose instead: StructuredOutput is the only
